---
layout: article
title: Zero
description: Create and manage Appwrite Zero projects from the CLI without an Appwrite account.
---

The `zero` command creates an [Appwrite Zero](/docs/zero) project without an account and links the current directory to it. The other `zero` commands check the time left, open the Console, extend the build window, list the Zero projects created on this machine, and delete a project.

{% info title="CLI version" %}
`appwrite zero` is available in Appwrite CLI version 28.15.0 and later. [Update your CLI](/docs/tooling/command-line/installation#update-your-cli) to the latest version before you start.
{% /info %}

# Create a project {% #create %}

Run `zero` in your app's directory, or pass a directory name to create a new one:

```sh
appwrite zero
appwrite zero my-app
```

The CLI writes `appwrite.config.json`, signs in to the new project, and prints its endpoint, ID, and claim link. Other commands, such as `appwrite push`, then work against the project.

{% info title="Active session" %}
Creating a Zero project makes its session the CLI's active one. To go back to your own account, run `appwrite login --switch`.
{% /info %}

# Check the time left {% #status %}

```sh
appwrite zero status
```

```text
projectId     : <PROJECT_ID>
status        : active
endpoint      : https://fra.cloud.appwrite.io/v1
buildTimeLeft : 49m
claimTimeLeft : 1d 49m
claimUrl      : https://appwrite.io/transfer?transferId=<TRANSFER_ID>&secret=<SECRET>
expiresAt     : 2026-11-25 08:02:16 UTC (in 49m)
claimBy       : 2026-11-26 08:02:16 UTC (in 1d)

ownerLinks
  https://<DOMAIN>.appwrite.network/__appwrite/zero?token=<TOKEN>
```

`ownerLinks` lists a link for each site and function domain. Open a link in a browser to access that domain's private deployment previews.

# Commands {% #commands %}

```sh
appwrite zero [directory] [options]
appwrite zero [command] [options]
```

{% table %}
* Command
* Description
---
* `zero [directory]`
* Create a Zero project and link the directory to it. Without a directory, uses the current one.
---
* `zero status`
* Show the time left to build and to claim, the claim link, and the owner links for the project's domains.
---
* `zero console`
* Open the project in the Console, signed in as its temporary owner. The link works once, for a few minutes.
---
* `zero extend`
* Add an hour to the build window, resuming a paused project. Works up to three times, never past the claim deadline.
---
* `zero list`
* List the Zero projects created on this machine, with the time left on each and its claim link.
---
* `zero delete`
* Delete the project before the claim deadline. Asks for confirmation unless `--force` is set.
{% /table %}

# Options {% #options %}

{% table %}
* Option
* Description
---
* `--region <region>`
* Create the project in a region: `fra`, `nyc`, `sfo`, `sgp`, `syd`, or `tor`. Defaults to the region closest to you.
---
* `--json`
* Print the result as JSON. On `zero`, this includes the claim link and the access token for private previews. On `zero console`, it prints the sign-in link without opening a browser.
---
* `--force`
* Skip the confirmation on `zero delete`, for agents and scripts.
{% /table %}
